==English==
{{was wotd|2006|August|29}}

===Pronunciation===
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-make a mountain out of a molehill.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-make a mountain out of a molehill.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|[[make]]<,,made> [[a]] [[mountain]] [[out of]] [[a]] [[molehill]]}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[treat#Verb|treat]] a [[problem]] as [[greater]] than it is; to [[blow out of proportion|blow something out of proportion]]; to [[exaggerate]] the [[importance]] of something [[trivial]].
#: {{ux|en|If you’re stuck in traffic, try not to '''make a mountain out of a molehill''' worrying about it too much. You could be making it much worse.}}
#* {{RQ:Lawrence Sons and Lovers|passage="It is only an old umbrella, isn't it?" she asked.|<br>She wondered why he, who did not usually trouble over trifles, '''made such a mountain of this molehill'''.|7}}

